Backport of SQLite check-in ad1bbfc2bd (trunk, 2026-09-29), "OPFS SAHPool:
more cleanly handle an init failure. Add an init option which tells it not to
wipe the storage if initialization fails", https://sqlite.org/src/info/ad1bbfc2bd,
forum report https://sqlite.org/forum/forumpost/5664cd4baee50236. GitHub
mirror commit ad1bbfc2bd1cb1c989d94fc1142fed4d72d42ec5. Code hunks are
upstream's ext/wasm/api/sqlite3-vfs-opfs-sahpool.c-pp.js diff verbatim,
retargeted at the built bundle (upstream's doc-only rewording of unrelated
methods is left out). Without it a failed setup (a reload's new Worker racing
the old Worker's still-closing access handles) calls removeVfs(), which deletes
every pool slot it can reach; the next setup finds a nonzero capacity, never
adds slots back, and the journal fails with "SAH pool is full".
Drop this patch once the pinned SQLite release contains ad1bbfc2bd.

